    - target: {fileID: 5250526870702089069, guid: 214324f6677dc394d81b5c93ccfefb88, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: The arrows are called "Ya". They are close to a meter or more and therefore
        really long in contrast to western counterparts. The arrowhead of this arrow
        is a traditional "Yajiri" and is not used in todays kyudo anymore. Todays
        arrowheads are designed more like bullets and are called "Yanone".
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
